    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0065" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/4–948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of
                        State, at Bogotá</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-04-15T12:00:00-05:00">April 15, 1948—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Telmar</hi> 66. With reference to the last para of
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Martel</hi> 28 of Apr 7 and to <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Martel</hi> 36 of Apr 9, FE and S/P<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d54-f1"/> are of the opinion that it would be unwise at this time to
                    reopen the question of so-called short-term <pb facs="0066" n="56" xml:id="pg56"
                    /> assistance to China, since the National Security Council has postponed
                    indefinitely its consideration of the problem.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d54-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>Unless you wish to press the Defense Establishment for clarification immediately,
                    Dept proposes to defer seeking suggested clarifications until it is prepared to
                    present basic paper on our position regarding China on which it is now
                    working.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d54-f1" n="90" xml:id="d54-f1-content">
                <p>Office of Far Eastern Affairs and Policy Planning Staff, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d54-f2" n="91" xml:id="d54-f2-content">
                <p>At a meeting on April 2 the National Security Council agreed that NSC6 had been
                    overtaken by events and deferred further action on the subject of China pending
                    receipt of a position paper from the Department of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
